heading":null},{"item_type":"experience","requirement_level":"required","item_text":"Minimum three (3) years of experience in a leadership role with or without direct reports.","source_heading":"Minimum Qualifications","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"job_duty","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Provides developmental opportunities for others; builds collaborative, cross-functional relationships. Solicits and acts on performance feedback; works closely with employees to set goals and provide open feedback and coaching to drive performance improvement.Pursues professional growth; develops and provides training and development to talent for growth opportunities; supports execution of performance management guidelines and expectations. Leads, adapts, implements, and stays up to date with organizational change, challenges, feedback, best practices, processes, and industry trends. Fosters open dialogue amongst team members, engages, motivates, and promotes collaboration within and across teams. Delegates tasks and decisions as appropriate; provides appropriate support, guidance, and scope; encourages development and consideration of options in decision making.","source_heading":"Essential Responsibilities","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"job_duty","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Manages designated work unit or team by translating business plans into tactical action items; oversees the completion of work assignments and identifies opportunities for improvement; ensures all policies and procedures are followed. Aligns team efforts; builds accountability for and measuring progress in achieving results; determines and ensures processes and methodologies are implemented; resolves escalated issues as appropriate; sets standards and measures progress. Fosters the development of work plans to meet business priorities and deadlines; obtains and distributes resources. Removes obstacles that impact performance; identifies and addresses improvement opportunities; guides performance and develops contingency plans accordingly; influences teams to execute in alignment with operational objectives.","source_heading":"Essential Responsibilities","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"job_duty","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Manages construction projects by: managing related financials to support accurate and timely budgets, cost estimates, and pre-construction services, while making recommendations for budget development; determining appropriate staffing of projects and managing staffing resources; monitoring project progress and completion to ensure project delivery within approved schedule and estimates; and evaluating major issues while collaborating with senior leaders to determine solutions and providing recommendations as needed.","source_heading":"Essential Responsibilities","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"job_duty","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Managing program performance by: assisting in evaluating and implementing construction metrics and performance monitoring; managing safety programs to ensure compliance with all regulatory and organizational standards; evaluating and planning solutions ensuring the adherence of facilities design standards; and identifying customer satisfaction and performance issues.","source_heading":"Essential Responsibilities","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"job_duty","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Managing vendor relationship management by: assessing current operational processes on an on-going basis while working with team to manage vendors, including vendor assessment and vendor performance analytics, to highlight trends and identify impactful process improvements that increase efficiency and effectiveness of vendor management; obtaining advanced research knowledge on vendor relationship management trends and applying strategies to business practices; and leads and manages the examination of financial qualifications, bonding capability, and safety records of potential vendors to be added to the Master Vendor list; and driving the team to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of vendor performance analytics and vendor assessment.","source_heading":"Essential Responsibilities","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Ambiguity/Uncertainty Management","source_heading":"Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: (Core)","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Architectural Engineering","source_heading":"Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: (Functional)","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Attention to Detail","source_heading":"Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: (Core)","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Building Regulatory Codes","source_heading":"Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: (Functional)","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Business Knowledge","source_heading":"Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: (Core)","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Construction","source_heading":"Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: (Functional)","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Communication","source_heading":"Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: (Core)","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Construction Drawings, Plans & Reports","source_heading":"Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: (Functional)","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Constructive Feedback","source_heading":"Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: (Core)","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Construction Finance","source_heading":"Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: (Functional)","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requir